Dates:
- If the document states when a policy was announced, comes/came into force,
  or becomes/became enforced, extract a Date node and connect it to the
  Policy with the matching edge type: announced_on, in_force_from, or
  enforced_from.
- Date node name: use the date as written in the source (e.g. "29 August 2023",
  "Summer 2023 (TBC)"). Do not normalize or reformat it.
- surface_form for the edge: the exact text stating the date relationship,
  copy-pasted verbatim.
- If a date is explicitly marked as provisional or unconfirmed (e.g. "TBC",
  "proposed", "expected"), still extract the edge, and set modality to
  "proposed" or "projected" rather than "in_force"/"enacted" -- do not drop
  the date just because it is uncertain.
- Do not extract a Date node for the document's own publication or
  sign-off date unless the document explicitly states it as the date the
  policy itself takes effect.
